  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="20">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 20</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="300" ed="#liebermann"/>Uton don eac georne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#ICn_20.lnote.oe.8"/>, swa we<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#ICn_20.lnote.oe.22"/> gyt læran wyllað: utan beon á urum hlaforde holde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#ICn_20.lnote.oe.23"/> ⁊ getrywe ⁊ æfre eallu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> mihtu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> his wurðscipe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#ICn_20.lnote.oe.24"/> ræran ⁊ his willan gewyrcan.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#ICn_20.lnote.oe.25"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="300" ed="#liebermann"/>Uton don eac georne, swá we gyt læran wyllað: uton beon á urum hlaforde holde ⁊ getréowe ⁊ æfre eallu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> mihtu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> his wurðscipe ræran ⁊ his willan gewyrcean.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="300" ed="#liebermann"/>Uton don eac, swa gyt we læran wyllað: uton beon á urum hlaforde holde ⁊ getrywe ⁊ æfre eallum mihtu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> his wurþscipes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_20.lnote.oe.2"/> ræran ⁊ his willan geweorcan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="20" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="301" ed="#liebermann"/>Item faciamus, sicut adhuc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_20.lnote.oe.6"/> persuadere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#ICn_20.lnote.oe.9"/> uolumus: simus dominis nostris<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_20.lnote.oe.6"/> per omnia fideles et credibiles et eorum gloriam totis uiribus exaltemus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#ICn_20.lnote.oe.10"/> et uelle faciamus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#ICn_20.lnote.oe.11"/>,</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="20" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="301" ed="#liebermann"/>Faciamus igitur quod adhuc docere uolumus: simus domino nostro semper fidi et fideles et totis uiribus nostris honorem eius sustineamus et uoluntatem eius impleamus.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="20" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="170" ed="#robertson"/>Uton don eac georne<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#ICn_20.robnote.fn.2"/> swá we gyt læran wyllað; uton beon á urum hlaforde holde ⁊ getréowe ⁊ æfre eallum mihtum his wurðscipe ræran ⁊ his willan gewyrcean.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="248" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Uton don eac georne, swa we gyt læran wyllað: utan beon a urum hlaforde holde and getrywe and æfre eallum mihtum his wurðscipe ræran and his willan gewyrcan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="301" ed="#liebermann"/>Lasst<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_20.lnote.de.1"/> uns auch willig handeln, wie wir nunmehr vorschreiben wollen: lasst uns stets unserem Herrn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_20.lnote.de.2"/> hold<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_20.lnote.de.3"/> und getreu sein und immer mit aller Macht seinen Ehrenrang<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_20.lnote.de.4"/> erhöhen und seinen Wunsch<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_20.lnote.de.3"/> ausführen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Let us also act eagerly, as we will now further instruct: let us always be loyal and faithful to our lord, and ever with all our might exalt his honour and do his will.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#ICn_20.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="171" ed="#robertson"/>Let us likewise zealously carry out what we further desire to enjoin: let us ever be faithful and true<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#ICn_20.robnote.n.2"/> to our lord, and always, with all our might, promote his honour and carry out his will.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="462" ed="#whitelock"/>Let us also perform zealously what we wish to enjoin further: let us ever be loyal and true to our lord and ever with all our might exalt his dignity and do his will.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="249" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Let us also do just as we further intend to instruct: let us always be faithful and true to our lord and ever with all our might uphold his sovereignty and carry out his will.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="301"><ref target="clause:Swer_1">Swer 1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Swer. 1 | ebd.</note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares Swer 1.; Robertson (p. 139) takes I Cn from B, which begins at ‘mæssedæg’ in 14.2, the earlier clauses being supplied from G; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 301, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">georne: omitted A</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_20.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">300</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_20.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">300</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gyt we l. wil.: uton <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gyt we l. wil.: uton Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_20.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">300</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ld <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ld Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_20.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">300</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-pes wæran <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-pes wæran Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_20.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">300</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-weor. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-weor. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_20.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">301</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_20.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">301</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ri <hi rend="italic">Dm R T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ri Dm R T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_20.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">301</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ex. et <hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ex. et lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_20.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">301</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">faciamus — fidelitate <hi rend="italic">überspringt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">faciamus — fidelitate skipped by K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_20.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">301</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-namus <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-namus Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_20.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">300</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_20.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">201</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">20—20, 2 benutzt durch <hi rend="italic">Hom. n</hi>. Wulfstan 119. 299. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Gefolge 10c</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">20—20, 2 used by <hi rend="italic">Hom. n</hi>. Wulfstan 119. 299. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Gefolge 10c</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_20.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">201</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">kinehlaford</hi> Hom. 119 in Einer Hs., aber nicht authentisch; <hi rend="italic">vgl. ebd</hi>.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">kinehlaford</hi> Hom. 119 in one MS, but not authentic; <hi rend="italic">cf. ibid</hi>.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_20.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">201</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Stücke der Formel des Mannschaftseides; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 2. e</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Parts of the formula of the oath of fealty; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 2. e</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_20.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">201</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘weltliche Grösse, gesellschaftliches Ansehen’ des Adels; ‘<hi rend="italic">gloria</hi>’ in Q zu abstrakt und ideal</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘worldly greatness, social standing’ of the nobility; ‘<hi rend="italic">gloria</hi>’ in Q is too abstract and idealized</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_20.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">350</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">With this clause and the two following, cf. Wulfstan, pp. 74, 119.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_20.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">350</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. <hi rend="italic">Oath Formulae</hi>, 1.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_20.robnote.fn.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">170</biblScope></bibl><label>man</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Om. A.</seg></note>
      </div>
